### Phone sign-in. All three routes are public (no token) and rate limited.
### Local test numbers never send an SMS: supabase/config.toml [auth.sms.test_otp]
### +1 555 555 0101 always accepts code 101010. (Only works if US is in auth.sms.allowed-countries.)

### 1. Start. Same response whether or not the number has an account.
# @name start
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/phone/start
Content-Type: application/json

{ "dialCode": "+1", "nationalNumber": "555 555 0101" }

###
@challengeId = {{start.response.body.$.challengeId}}

### 2. Verify with the right code -> { session: { accessToken, refreshToken, expiresAt }, isNewUser }
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/phone/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "challengeId": "{{challengeId}}", "code": "101010" }

### 2b. Wrong code -> 400 WRONG_CODE with attemptsLeft (2, 1, 0). The next call is 423 LOCKED with Retry-After.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/phone/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "challengeId": "{{challengeId}}", "code": "000000" }

### 3. Resend. 60 s cooldown (429 + Retry-After before that) and the hourly limits apply.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/phone/resend
Content-Type: application/json

{ "challengeId": "{{challengeId}}" }

### Rejections
### 400 INVALID_PHONE
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/phone/start
Content-Type: application/json

{ "dialCode": "+234", "nationalNumber": "123" }

### 400 COUNTRY_NOT_SUPPORTED (France is not in the default allow-list)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/phone/start
Content-Type: application/json

{ "dialCode": "+33", "nationalNumber": "6 12 34 56 78" }

### 404 CHALLENGE_NOT_FOUND
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/phone/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "challengeId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000", "code": "123456" }

### /auth/phone/call is not implemented (decision 12): 401 without a token, 404 with one.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/phone/call
Content-Type: application/json

{}
